<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    7.4.1: Comparing Expressions
  </item>
  <item>
    7.4.2: Exploring Linear, Exponential, and Quadratic Growth
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      7.4.2: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      7.4.2: Additional Resources
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    7.4.3: Comparing Exponential and Quadratic Functions
  </item>
  <list>
    <item>
      7.4.3: Self Check
    </item>
    <item>
      7.4.3: Additional Resources
    </item>
  </list>
  <item>
    7.4.4: Comparing Exponential and Quadratic Expressions
  </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 7.4.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>
    Graphing technology
  </item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their
  own device.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for
    these words and notice their use and meanings.
  </item>
  <item>
    Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>
    Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>
  </item>
</list>
